    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "The Adventures of Tom Sawyer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was written in 1876. It is one of the best-loved works of American author Mark Twain."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Tom Sawyer is a young boy. The thing he seems to enjoy most is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "getting into trouble",
            "ref": "v-get-into-trouble"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One day, Tom and his friend Huckleberry Finn decide to meet in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "graveyard",
            "zh": "墓地"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at midnight to test a method of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "curing",
            "ref": "v-cure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a skin disease. At the graveyard, they "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "witness",
            "ref": "v-witness"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "murder",
            "ref": "v-murder"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Injun Joe kills Dr. Robinson and tries to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "blame",
            "ref": "v-blame"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it on the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "drunken",
            "zh": "喝醉的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Muff Porter. Injun Joe doesn’t know that the boys have seen what he’s done."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Huckleberry and Tom decide not to tell anyone what they have seen because they are afraid that Injun Joe will hurt them. However, Tom feels bad when Muff goes to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "jail",
            "ref": "v-jail"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for Robinson’s murder."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Finally, Tom decides to tell everyone the truth. Thanks to him, Muff is released. However, Injun Joe escapes through a window. In the final part of the novel, Injun Joe dies inside a cave. Tom and Huckleberry later discover his box of gold."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
